{% comment %}
  ============================================================================
  Learn Page — "Step-by-Step Guides" (task 0007, round 2 — replaces the native
  featured-blog-posts instance previously used here)
  ============================================================================
  DXB asked for this section to match production's real card look (icon badge + title +
  description + a single "X min read" badge). Checked https://buyflorabella.com/learn directly:
  production's live Guides cards do NOT show a separate difficulty-level badge — that field only
  ever existed in the old Hydrogen static mock data (staticData.ts's `guides` export), not in
  what's actually live now. So this only needs read time, not difficulty, matching reality
  rather than the stale mock.

  Pulls real articles from a real Shopify Blog via a native `"type": "blog"` picker setting
  (left blank by default — DXB assigns the "Guides" blog in the theme editor, same reasoning as
  the Articles section: after this session's sync troubles, resource-reference values are always
  left for Admin's native picker rather than guessed at in code).

  CARD MARKUP lives in snippets/bfbella-guide-card.liquid (render, not a theme block) — the
  per-article read time is computed here and passed in, which only a snippet (not a theme block)
  supports passing.

  READ TIME: not a native Article field. Estimated from word count (~200 words/minute, floored
  at 1) — an approximation, not a real per-article value, same technique already used on the
  Articles section above.

  ORDERING (round 4 — re-applied after Admin reverted round 3's fix): guide left-to-right order
  comes from tagging each article "featured1"/"featured2"/.../"featuredN" (prefix configurable
  via order_tag_prefix). The original attempt sorted a computed key string built with
  prepend/slice tricks, then re-matched handles back to articles — fragile, and it broke down to
  showing only one guide once real tag data was involved. Round 3 replaced this with a simpler
  exact-match approach (scan for an article whose tags contain, case-insensitively, the exact
  "featured<N>" string — never a substring/prefix check). That fix was live and correct, but
  Shopify's Admin "Edit code" editor reverted this entire file back to the original broken
  version in a later sync commit (confirmed via `git log` — a stale in-browser copy got
  re-saved, overwriting the fix; same class of issue as the template-JSON wipes documented in
  LEARN_PAGE_ADMIN_GUIDE.md, now confirmed to also hit section *code*, not just settings data).
  Round 4 re-applies the exact-match fix and adds an `enable_ordering` checkbox (default on) so
  DXB can rule ordering in/out as a variable when debugging without needing a code change —
  unchecked, this section just shows the first `post_limit` guides in the blog's own order, no
  tag logic at all.

  ROUND 5 (still 2026-09-07): round 4's exact-match logic was confirmed correct in code, and
  confirmed to be the actual deployed version this time (checked git log, not just memory) — yet
  a direct curl fetch of the live page (cookie-jar method, per this project's own established
  verification pattern) showed only ONE guide card rendering, matching the first tagged
  position, with `enable_ordering` and `order_tag_prefix` both confirmed correctly set. Round 4's
  logic used three levels of nested `for` loops (position → article → tag) with `break`/
  `continue` inside the two inner levels; rewrote it to use `unless`/boolean flags instead,
  suspecting the break/continue nesting depth itself as the cause.

  ROUND 6 (still 2026-09-07, the actual root cause): DXB's own VS Code Liquid extension flagged
  the real bug directly — round 5 introduced `assign already_shown = shown_handles contains
  article.handle` (twice). This is invalid Liquid: `contains` (like `==`, `and`, `or`) is only
  valid inside a conditional tag's expression (`if`/`unless`/`case`), never on the right-hand
  side of `assign` — Liquid's assign grammar only accepts a variable, a literal, or a filtered
  chain (`| filter: arg`), not a general boolean expression. This is the exact same class of
  parse-time grammar violation as the earlier piped-filter-in-a-for-tag bug from task 0009 (see
  CLAUDE.md's "Liquid Syntax Gotchas") — invalid in a way none of this project's own checks (JSON
  schema validation, tag balance/nesting counting) can catch, since it's not a structural
  mismatch, it's a grammar rule about which tags accept which kinds of expressions. Fixed by
  moving the `contains` check directly into the enclosing `unless` condition instead of assigning
  its result to a variable first (`unless found_this_position or shown_handles contains
  article.handle`) — `contains` combined with `and`/`or` inside an `if`/`unless` IS valid, only
  assigning its bare result to a variable isn't. Round 4/5's break/continue rewrite reasoning
  above may well have been chasing the wrong culprit the whole time; this is the fix that
  actually matches a concrete, tool-confirmed diagnosis rather than another plausible-sounding
  theory.

  COLOR: no hardcoded hex. Accent resolves through section.settings.accent_color, falling back
  to color_palette.color3. Background falls back to color_palette.background.

  DEPLOY: written directly into this live repo's working tree as part of the 2026-09-07
  live-edit pilot (see claude_docs/build_docs/live_edit_pilot_plan.md) — DXB reviews, then
  commits and pushes by hand.
  ============================================================================
{% endcomment %}

{% liquid
  assign accent = section.settings.accent_color | default: settings.color_palette.color3
  assign bg = section.settings.background_color | default: settings.color_palette.background
  assign card_bg = section.settings.card_background_color | default: settings.color_palette.background
  assign card_heading_color = section.settings.card_heading_color | default: settings.color_palette.foreground
  assign card_text_color = section.settings.card_text_color | default: settings.color_palette.foreground

  if section.settings.background_color != blank
    render 'contrast-override', background_color: section.settings.background_color, section_id: section.id, skip_contrast: true
  endif
%}

<div
  id="LearnGuides-{{ section.id }}"
  class="bfbella-learn-guides{% if section.settings.background_color != blank %} color-custom-{{ section.id }}{% endif %}"
  style="
    --bfbella-accent: {{ accent }};
    --bfbella-bg: {{ bg }};
    --bfbella-card-bg: {{ card_bg }};
    --bfbella-card-heading-color: {{ card_heading_color }};
    --bfbella-card-text-color: {{ card_text_color }};
    {% if section.settings.padding_top != blank %}--bfbella-pad-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top }}px;{% endif %}
    {% if section.settings.padding_bottom != blank %}--bfbella-pad-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom }}px;{% endif %}
  "
>
  <div class="bfbella-learn-guides__inner page-width">
    {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
      <h2 class="bfbella-learn-guides__heading">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.settings.guides_blog != blank -%}
      <div class="bfbella-learn-guides__grid">
        {%- if section.settings.enable_ordering == false -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign max_shown = section.settings.post_limit | default: 3
            for article in section.settings.guides_blog.articles limit: max_shown
              assign word_count = article.content | strip_html | split: ' ' | size
              assign read_minutes = word_count | divided_by: 200
              assign read_minutes = read_minutes | at_least: 1
              render 'bfbella-guide-card', article: article, read_minutes: read_minutes
            endfor
          -%}
        {%- else -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign order_prefix = section.settings.order_tag_prefix | default: 'featured' | downcase
            assign max_shown = section.settings.post_limit | default: 3
            assign shown_handles = '|'
            assign shown_count = 0

            for n in (1..12)
              unless shown_count >= max_shown
                assign target_tag = order_prefix | append: n
                assign found_this_position = false

                for article in section.settings.guides_blog.articles
                  unless found_this_position or shown_handles contains article.handle
                    assign matched = false
                    for tag in article.tags
                      assign tag_downcase = tag | downcase
                      if tag_downcase == target_tag
                        assign matched = true
                      endif
                    endfor

                    if matched
                      assign shown_handles = shown_handles | append: article.handle | append: '|'
                      assign shown_count = shown_count | plus: 1
                      assign found_this_position = true
                      assign word_count = article.content | strip_html | split: ' ' | size
                      assign read_minutes = word_count | divided_by: 200
                      assign read_minutes = read_minutes | at_least: 1
                      render 'bfbella-guide-card', article: article, read_minutes: read_minutes
                    endif
                  endunless
                endfor
              endunless
            endfor

            for article in section.settings.guides_blog.articles
              unless shown_count >= max_shown or shown_handles contains article.handle
                assign shown_handles = shown_handles | append: article.handle | append: '|'
                assign shown_count = shown_count | plus: 1
                assign word_count = article.content | strip_html | split: ' ' | size
                assign read_minutes = word_count | divided_by: 200
                assign read_minutes = read_minutes | at_least: 1
                render 'bfbella-guide-card', article: article, read_minutes: read_minutes
              endunless
            endfor
          -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  .bfbella-learn-guides {
    position: relative;
    padding-block-start: var(--bfbella-pad-top, 4rem);
    padding-block-end: var(--bfbella-pad-bottom, 4rem);
    background-color: var(--bfbella-bg);
    color: var(--color-foreground);
  }

  .bfbella-learn-guides__inner {
    max-width: 80rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-inline: 1.5rem;
  }

  .bfbella-learn-guides__heading {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-block-end: 2rem;
  }

  .bfbella-learn-guides__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;

    @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "BFBella — Learn Guides",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section-wrapper",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Content"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "Step-by-Step Guides"
    },
    {
      "type": "blog",
      "id": "guides_blog",
      "label": "Guides blog"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "post_limit",
      "label": "Number of guides to show",
      "min": 1,
      "max": 12,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "enable_ordering",
      "label": "Enable tag-based ordering",
      "default": true,
      "info": "Debug/developer toggle. Uncheck to bypass tag-based ordering entirely and just show the first guides in the blog's own order — useful for isolating whether an issue is in the ordering logic or somewhere else."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "order_tag_prefix",
      "label": "Ordering tag prefix",
      "default": "featured",
      "info": "Tag each guide article with this prefix plus a number (e.g. \"featured1\", \"featured2\", \"featured3\") to control left-to-right order. Guides without a matching tag show last, in their normal blog order.",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.enable_ordering }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Appearance"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "accent_color",
      "label": "Accent color",
      "placeholder": "t:settings.default",
      "info": "Leave blank to use the theme's existing color3 (brand green) swatch."
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "background_color",
      "label": "Background color",
      "placeholder": "t:settings.default",
      "info": "The outer section, behind the cards."
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "card_background_color",
      "label": "Card background color",
      "placeholder": "t:settings.default",
      "info": "Each guide card's own background — independent from the section background above."
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "card_heading_color",
      "label": "Card heading color",
      "placeholder": "t:settings.default"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "card_text_color",
      "label": "Card text color",
      "placeholder": "t:settings.default",
      "info": "Applies to the description and read-time text."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Padding"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "label": "Top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 200,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 64
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "label": "Bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 200,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 64
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "BFBella — Learn Guides",
      "category": "Custom"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
